r **all real numbers**, because the cube of a negative number is negative, and the cube of a positive number is positive. Thus, the cube root is defined for:\n\n$$\nx \\in \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Combine the Restrictions\n\nThe only restriction comes from the square root term, which requires $ x \\geq 2 $. The cube root term imposes no restriction on $ x $, so the entire function is defined for:\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{[2, \\infty)}\n$$<|im_end|><|im_end|>\n"], label: [2,\infty), reward: 1.0
